WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
In the Western Han, Su Wu was sent by the Han court on a mission to the Xiongnu.

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.620
Holding his envoy's staff, he set out from Chang'an.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.990
When he reached the Xiongnu, he was detained because of a political incident.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.300
He stood straight and tall, preferring death to surrender.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:20.940
He was exiled to the north to herd sheep, always gripping his envoy's staff tightly.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:29.930
In the bitter winter, he herded sheep in a world of ice and snow, eating snow to stave off hunger, the flock huddled beside him.

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:37.680
Spring went and autumn came, and the years slipped by. His hair gradually whitened, but the staff was still held high.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.380
Many years later, he finally returned to Han.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:47.400
'Su Wu herding sheep' became a famous story of holding to one's mission and to loyalty.

